Windows: seven rustkit-engine tests fail here on a hardware GPU and on the software adapter alike
(refresh #20, found by the chunked engine run; RTX 4090 and forced WARP give the same result).
They are not adapter failures; each is a Windows parity gap with its own row:

  Windows parity row (web fonts): DirectWrite shapes text in the system face (Segoe UI) rather
  than the page's installed web face (Ahem, Noto Sans), so these assert a face or its pixels and fail:
    incremental_layout_tests::a_web_font_landing_after_layout_measures_text_afresh
    paint_only_web_font_tests::a_committed_frame_draws_its_web_font_on_a_thread_that_did_not_install_it
    paint_only_web_font_tests::an_element_scroll_keeps_the_web_font_when_another_view_painted
    paint_only_web_font_tests::static_text_keeps_its_web_font_across_paint_only_frames_when_another_view_paints
    paint_only_web_font_tests::web_faces_hold_by_weight_when_another_view_on_the_thread_paints
    paint_only_web_font_tests::web_faces_hold_while_another_thread_installs_its_own
  Windows parity row (dom1 1 px):
    dom1_attr_order_hit_tests::a_box_outside_its_ancestors_box_is_hit (rect menu y 285, Chromium 284)

Each is ignored on Windows with the row in its reason. Remove each hunk when its row lands.

